Folios License
Version 1.0, October 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 ixDarkLorD.

Folios is free to use, and you may reuse its code, change it and publish forks of it, as long as you credit its
author (section 4). What this license does not allow, it reserves to the author. If something you want to do is not
covered here, ask: https://github.com/ixDarkLorD


1. Definitions

  "Folios" means the Folios mod: its source code, compiled files (jars), assets (textures, models, sounds, fonts,
  translations, shaders) and documentation, in every version, on every loader and platform.

  "The Template" means the example resource pack in the folder templates/folios-book-template of the Folios source,
  and any copy of it published by the author. It is not covered by this license (see section 6).

  "Addon" means a separate mod, plugin, datapack or program that works with Folios, uses its public API
  (net.ixdarklord.folios.api) or its file formats, and does not contain Folios's code or assets.

  "Content" means guide books, resource packs, data packs, translations and other files that Folios reads, made by
  you.

  "Derived work" means anything that contains Folios's code or assets, in whole or in part, changed or not: a fork,
  a modified version, a port to another game version or loader, or another project that reuses parts of Folios.

  "Official source" means the Folios project pages on CurseForge and Modrinth, its website
  (https://ixdarklord.github.io/Folios/), and any other place the author names.


2. What you may do without asking

  a. Use. Download Folios from an official source and use it, in single player, on servers and anywhere else you
     play Minecraft.

  b. Modpacks. Include Folios in modpacks, public or private, free or monetized through a platform's own reward
     program (such as CurseForge's or Modrinth's). Where the platform can fetch Folios from an official source (a
     Modrinth .mrpack, a CurseForge manifest), use that rather than a copy of the jar. Where it cannot, you may
     include the unmodified jar, as long as the pack credits Folios and links to an official source.

  c. Addons. Make, publish and sell Addons, under any license you choose. You may compile against the Folios jar
     and depend on it, and tell your users to install it from an official source.

  d. Content. Make, publish and sell Content: books, resource packs, data packs and translations for Folios. A
     resource pack may contain changed versions of Folios's own textures, models, sounds and translations, for the
     purpose of restyling or translating Folios.

  e. Media. Show Folios in videos, streams, screenshots, articles and reviews, monetized or not.

  f. Code and assets. Copy, study, change and reuse Folios's code and assets, in whole or in part, in your own
     projects, open or closed source, free or paid, under any license you choose, as long as you give credit as
     section 4 asks.

  g. Forks. Publish modified versions and forks of Folios, including ports to other game versions and loaders, as
     long as you give credit as section 4 asks and the fork has a name and a mod id of its own (section 3c).

  h. Contributing. Changes you send the author may be used by the author in Folios, under this license, without
     further permission.


3. What you may not do without the author's written permission

  a. Re-upload Folios unchanged, mirror it, or bundle it with anything other than a modpack (section 2b). Point
     people to an official source instead.

  b. Sell Folios itself unchanged, or put it behind a paywall, a download gate or an ad-link service.

  c. Publish a Derived work under the name "Folios", with Folios's mod id ("folios") or logo, or in any way that
     presents it as Folios itself or as made or endorsed by the author.

  d. Present Folios, or a part of it, as your own work, or remove or change its copyright and license notices.


4. Credit

  Every Derived work must credit Folios and its author. This is a condition of sections 2f and 2g: without the
  credit, those permissions do not apply.

  a. Where people see it. Name Folios and its author, ixDarkLorD, with a link to an official source, on the
     Derived work's project page (its description on CurseForge, Modrinth or wherever it is published) and in its
     README. For example: "Based on Folios by ixDarkLorD (https://ixdarklord.github.io/Folios/)".

  b. In the mod. If the Derived work is a mod, name Folios and ixDarkLorD in its metadata's credits (the
     "contributors" or "authors" of fabric.mod.json, the "credits" of mods.toml or neoforge.mods.toml).

  c. In the source. Keep this license's copyright line with the code you took, and include a copy of this license,
     or a link to it, in the Derived work's source.

  d. Say what changed. A fork or modified version must say that it is changed from Folios.

  Addons, Content, modpacks and media do not need this credit (beyond what section 2b asks of modpacks), though it
  is always welcome.


5. Conditions

  a. These permissions last as long as you keep to this license. If you break it, they end for you, and are
     restored only if the author agrees.

  b. You must also follow the Minecraft End User License Agreement and Usage Guidelines.

  c. Folios depends on CoolCatLib, a separate mod with its own license. This license covers Folios only.


